$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for cross-coupling of terminal or alkyl-substituted
cyclopropyl silanols:
1-((1S,2R)-2-(2-(Benzyloxy)ethyl)cyclopropyl)-3-chlorobenzene (8g) 6g
(367 mg, 1.0 mmol) was treated with neat BF3·OEt2 (0.12 mL, 1.0 mmol) for
15 min. THF (2.5 mL) was added and the mixture was transferred to a
crimped microwave flask charged with Pd(PPh3)4 (29 mg, 5 mol %).
3-Chlorobenzene (59 µL, 0.5 mmol) was added followed by TBAF (2.0 mL, 2.0
mmol, 1M in THF). The reaction was heated to 100 °C for 16 h. The mixture
was concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was dissolved in
CH2Cl2 and filtered over a short pad of silica gel. After concentration
in vacuo the crude product was purified by flash chromatography (39:1
Hexanes/EtOAc) yielding the title compound (114.0 mg, 80 %) as a
colorless oil. Rf: 0.30 (9:1 Hexanes/EtOAc). 1H-NMR(CDCl3, 400 MHz):
7.38-7.26 (m, 5H), 7.19-7.01 (m, 2H), 7.02-7.00 (m, 1H), 6.93-6.90 (m,
1H), 4.54 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 4.51 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H) 3.59 (t, J =
6.5 Hz, 2H), 1.75-1.63 (m, 3H), 1.19-1.11 (m, 1H), 0.93-0.0.88 (m, 1H)
0.86-0.81 (m, 1H). 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): 145.8, 138.4, 134.0, 129.3,
128.3, 127.5, 127.4, 125.8, 125.3, 123.9, 72.9, 69.9, 34.4, 22.7, 21.0,
16.0. IR (film): 2854, 1598, 1453, 1099, 1027, 781, 732, 691 cm-1. HRMS
(ESI, Pos) calcd for C18H19Cl1O1 [M+ H]+: 287.1203 m/z, found 287.1197
m/z.
