$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure C: Ethyl
4-((1S,2S)-2-(3-chlorophenyl)cyclopropyl)benzoate (8b)
3-((1S,2S)-2-o-Tolylcyclopropyl)pyridine (8e) The product was prepared by
the general procedure C using 242 mg of 6e (0.75 mmol). The crude product
was purified by flash chromatography (1:1 Et2O/Hexanes -3:2 Et2O/Hexanes)
affording the title compound (82 mg, 79%) as a pale yellow oil. Rf: 0.32
(3:2 EtOAc/Hexanes). 1H-NMR(CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 8.54-8.44 (m, 2H),
7.44-7.40 (m, 1H), 7.25-7.08 (m, 5H), 2.33 (s, 3H), 2.25-2.19 (m, 1H),
2.05-2.00 (m, 1H), 1.57-1.52 (m, 1H), 1.44-1.39 (m, 1H). 13C-NMR(CDCl3,
75 MHz): δ 148.0, 147.0, 139.3, 138.3, 137.8, 132.3, 129.7, 126.3, 125.9,
125.5, 123.3, 26.1, 23.2, 19.8, 16.0. IR (film): 3021, 1572, 1480, 1456,
1424, 1024, 756, 731, 711, 630 cm-1. HRMS (ESI, Pos) calcd for C15H16N1
[M+H]+: 210.1285 m/z, found 210.1277 m/z.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Hiyama-Denmark Cross-Coupling reaction
