$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Cross-Coupling Procedure with P(t-Bu)2Me. In a glove box, P(t-Bu)2Me (16
mg, 0.10 mmol).was added to a suspension of PdBr2 (10.6 mg, 0.040 mmol)
in THF (2.4 mL). This mixture was stirred for 30 minutes, and to this
homogeneous orange-yellow solution was added (MeO)3SiPh (224 µL, 1.20
mmol), TBAF (2.4 mL, 2.4 mmol), and the alkyl halide (1.00 mmol). The
resulting mixture was stirred vigorously for 14 hours at room
temperature. The reaction mixture was then filtered through a short pad
of silica gel (washed with ~100 mL of Et2O or EtOAc), concentrated, and
purified by column chromatography.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimized on cat.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Room-Temperature Hiyama Cross-Couplings of Arylsilanes with Alkyl
Bromides and Iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
