$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.3. General procedure A (in the Presence of
Ligand PN-1, Table 2) 4-Chloro-4’-methylbiphenyl (c10): The title
compound c10 was prepared following the general procedure A from the
reaction of (p-chlorophenyl)triethoxysilane with piodotoluene for 24 h
and obtained as a white solid (150 mg, 74% yield) after purification by
silica gel column chromatography using hexanes as an eluting solvent. 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.42 (s, 3H), 7.28 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 7.41 (dd,
J = 8.4, 1.8 Hz, 2H), 7.48 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 7.54 (dd, J = 8.4, 1.8
Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 21.2, 126.9, 128.3, 129.0, 129.7,
133.1, 137.2, 137.6, 139.7; HRMS (APCI) Calcd for C13H11Cl (M)+ 202.0549,
found 202.0543.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Hiyama coupling, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper-Catalyzed Hiyama Coupling of (Hetero)aryltriethoxysilanes with
(Hetero)aryl Iodides
