$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.3. General procedure A (in the Presence of
Ligand PN-1, Table 2) 4-Methoxybiphenyl (c7): The title compound c7 was
prepared following the general procedure A from the reaction of
phenyltriethoxysilane with p-iodoanisole for 24 h and obtained as a white
solid (87 mg, 47% yield) after purification by silica gel column
chromatography using hexanes as an eluting solvent. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 3.87 (s, 3H), 7.00 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 7.32 (t, J = 7.2 Hz,
1H), 7.43 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 7.55 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (75MHz, CDCl3) δ
55.5, 114.3, 126.8, 126.9, 128.3, 128.9, 133.9, 141.0, 159.3; HRMS (APCI)
Calcd for C13H13O (MH)+ 185.0966, found 185.0964.
