$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 2-Phenyl-1,3-Butadiene (15) under Domino Reaction
Conditions. Diene - 2 (0.108 g, 0.502 mmol), N-Phenylmaleimide (0.107 g,
0.618 mmol), 0.5M TBAF solution (0.93 mL, 0.465 mmol), PdCl2(PPh3)2
(0.005 g, 1.5 mol %), CuI (0.015 g, 0.079 mmol) and iodobenzene (0.102 g,
0.502 mmol) were taken into a thick walled microwave tube equipped with a
stir-bar. The contents were added with THF (2.0 mL) and the sealed tube
was left at room temperature for 36h with constant stirring. The reaction
mixture was added to Et2O (10 mL) and quenched with 1.2M HCl (10 mL) and
filtered through a pad of silica to remove solid particulate matter. The
silica pad was washed with Et2O (2 × 10 mL), and the resulting filtrate
was washed successively with 1.2M HCl (2 × 25 mL), water (2 × 25 mL) and
dried over MgSO4. After removal of volatiles, the crude product was
purified by flash chromatography producing compound 15 as a
yellowish-brown oil (0.047 g, 0.361 mmol, 72.3 %). The spectral data for
this compound (15) was consistent with that previously reported.9
Synthesis of 2-Phenyl-1,3-Butadiene (15). Yield(0.047 g, 0.361 mmol, 72.3
%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Hiyama cross-coupling reaction, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
