$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2.3. General procedure A (in the Presence of Ligand PN-1, Table 2) In a
glovebox, aryl iodide (1.0 mmol), CsF (228 mg, 1.5 mmol), CuI (19.0 mg,
0.10 mmol) and PN-1 ligand (30 mg, 0.10 mmol) were weighed in a 4 dram
borosilicate scintillation vial and dissolved in DMF (5 mL).
Aryltriethoxysilane (1.0 mmol) was then added to the reaction mixture,
tightly capped with a poly-seal cone-lined urea cap (Wheaton). The
reaction mixture was taken out of the glovebox and placed in an oil bath
pre-heated to 120 °C with vigorous stirring. After 24 h (Table 2) or 12 h
(Table 3), the reaction mixture was cooled down to room temperature,
diluted with H2O (10 mL) and extracted with ethyl acetate (5 mL × 3). The
combined organic fraction was dried over Na2SO4, cotton-filtered and the
solvent was removed in a rotary evaporator. The product was purified by
silica gel column chromatography using hexanes and a combination of
hexanes with diethyl ether or ethyl acetate (see below at respective
products for exact solvent combinations) as an eluting solvent.
