$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Cross-Coupling Procedure with
[HP(t-Bu)2Me]BF4. In the air, PdBr2 (10.6 mg, 0.040 mmol) and
[HP(t-Bu)2Me]BF4 (24.8 mg, 0.10 mmol) were placed in a vial equipped with
a stir bar. The vial was closed with a septum screw-cap, and then it was
evacuated and refilled with argon (three times). THF (2.4 mL) and TBAF
(0.10 mL, 0.10 mmol) were added, and the resulting mixture was stirred
vigorously for 30 minutes at room temperature. To the resulting
homogeneous orange-yellow solution was added (MeO)3SiPh (224 µL, 1.20
mmol), TBAF (2.3 mL, 2.3 mmol), and the alkyl bromide (1.00 mmol). The
reaction mixture was stirred vigorously for 14 hours at room temperature.
The reaction mixture was then filtered through a short pad of silica gel
(washed with ~100 mL of Et2O or EtOAc), concentrated, and purified by
column chromatography. entry 6; Yield: 42%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
