$DATUM 2.4. General Procedure B (in the Absence of Ligand, Table 3) In a
glovebox, aryl iodide (1.0 mmol), CsF (228 mg, 1.5 mmol) and CuI (19.0
mg, 0.1 mmol) were weighed in a 4 dram borosilicate scintillation vial
and dissolved in DMF (5 mL). Aryltriethoxysilane (1.0 mmol) was then
added to the reaction mixture, tightly capped with a poly-seal cone-lined
urea cap (Wheaton). The reaction mixture was taken out of the glovebox
and placed in an oil bath pre-heated to 120 °C with vigorous stirring.
After 24 h (Table 2) or 12 h (Table 3), the reaction mixture was cooled
down to room temperature, diluted with H2O (10 mL) and extracted with
ethyl acetate (5 mL× 3). The combined organic fraction was dried over
Na2SO4, cotton-filtered and the solvent was removed in a rotary
evaporator. The product was purified by silica gel column chromatography
using hexanes and a combination of hexanes and ethyl acetate (see below
at respective products for exact solvent combinations) as an eluting
solvent. 2-Phenylpyridine (c14): The title compound c14 was prepared
following the general procedure B from the reaction of
phenyltriethoxysilane with o-iodopyridine for 12 h and obtained as oil
(100 mg, 64% yield) after purification by silica gel column
chromatography using 10% ethyl acetate in hexanes as an eluting solvent.
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.28 (m, 1H), 7.50 (m, 3H), 7.77 (s, 2H), 8.04
(d, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 8.74 (d, J = 4.5 Hz, 1H) ; 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
120.6, 122.2, 127.0, 128.8, 129.0, 136.8, 139.5, 149.7, 157.5; HRMS
(APCI) Calcd for C11H10N (MH)+ 156.0813, found 156.0810.
