$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure C: Ethyl
4-((1S,2S)-2-(3-chlorophenyl)cyclopropyl)benzoate (8b)
1-(4-((1S,2S)-2-Butylcyclopropyl)phenyl)ethanone (8f) The product was
prepared by the general procedure C using 58 mg of 6f (0.2 mmol). The
crude product was purified by flash chromatography (19:1 Hexanes/EtOAc)
affording the desired product (68 mg, 63%) as a clear oil. Rf: 23 (9:1
Hexanes/EtOAc). 1H-NMR(CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 7.83-7.79 (m, 2H), 7.08-7.04
(m, 2H), 2.53 (s, 3H), 1.66-1.59 (m, 1H), 1.42-1.27 (m, 6H), 1.11-1.01
(m, 1H), 0.97-0.81 (m, 5H). 13CNMR(CDCl3, 75 MHz): 197.6, 150.5, 134.3,
128.4, 125.3, 34.0, 31.5, 26.5, 25.2, 23.5, 22.4, 17.4, 14.1. IR (film):
2922, 1677, 1604, 1356, 1266, 1181, 954, 829, 594 cm-1. HRMS (ESI, Pos)
calcd for C15H21O1 [M+H]+: 217.1587 m/z, found 217.1587 m/z.
