$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.4. General Procedure B (in the Absence of
Ligand, Table 3) In a glovebox, aryl iodide (1.0 mmol), CsF (228 mg, 1.5
mmol) and CuI (19.0 mg, 0.1 mmol) were weighed in a 4 dram borosilicate
scintillation vial and dissolved in DMF (5 mL). Aryltriethoxysilane (1.0
mmol) was then added to the reaction mixture, tightly capped with a
poly-seal cone-lined urea cap (Wheaton). The reaction mixture was taken
out of the glovebox and placed in an oil bath pre-heated to 120 °C with
vigorous stirring. After 24 h (Table 2) or 12 h (Table 3), the reaction
mixture was cooled down to room temperature, diluted with H2O (10 mL) and
extracted with ethyl acetate (5 mL× 3). The combined organic fraction was
dried over Na2SO4, cotton-filtered and the solvent was removed in a
rotary evaporator. The product was purified by silica gel column
chromatography using hexanes and a combination of hexanes and ethyl
acetate (see below at respective products for exact solvent combinations)
as an eluting solvent. 2-(4-Methoxyphenyl)pyridine (c19): The title
compound c19 was prepared following the general procedure B from the
reaction of (p-methoxyphenyl)triethoxysilane with oiodopyridine for 12 h
and obtained as white solid (109 mg, 59% yield) after purification by
silica gel column chromatography using 10% ethyl acetate in hexanes as an
eluting solvent. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.86 (s, 3H). 7.00 (d, J =
7.8, 2H), 7.16 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 1H), 7.69 (m, 2H), 7.95 (dd, J = 6.9, 2.1
Hz, 2H), 8.65 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 55.5, 114.2,
119.9, 121.5, 128.3, 132.2, 136.8, 149.7, 157.2, 160.6; HRMS (ESI) Calcd
for C12H12NO (MH)+ 186.0919, found 186.0913.
