$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.3. General procedure A (in the Presence of
Ligand PN-1, Table 2) 4-Methoxy-4’-trifluoromethylbiphenyl (c12): The
title compound c12 was prepared following the general procedure A from
the reaction of (p-methoxylphenyl)triethoxysilane with
p-iodobenzotrifluoride for 24 h and obtained as a white solid (129 mg,
51% yield) after purification by silica gel column chromatography using
hexanes as an eluting solvent. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.87 (s, 3H),
7.00 (dd, J = 6.9, 2.1 Hz, 2H), 7.55 (dd, J = 6.9, 2.1 Hz, 2H), 7.67 (m,
4H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 55.5, 114.6, 125.8 (d, J CF = 3.5 Hz),
127.0, 128.5, 132.3, 144.4, 160.0; 19F NMR (282 Hz, CDCl3) δ -60.8; HRMS
(APCI) Calcd for C14H11F3O (M)+ 252.0762, found 252.0764.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Hiyama coupling, sealed tube used
