$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A: To a stirred solution of
siloxane 1 or benzylic alcohol 8 (0.5 mmol) in dry THF (2.0 mL) at -78 °C
was added MeLi in Et2O (0.6 mmol), dropwise. The reaction mixture was
allowed to warm to room temperature and was stirred for 1 h. HMPA (1 mL,
freshly distilled) was added followed by CuI (114 mg, 0.6 mmol). The
slurry was allowed to obtain homogenaiety over 1 h, and a solution of
Pd(PPh3)4 (17 mg, 0.02 mmol) and Ar-I (1.0 mmol) in dry THF (1 mL) was
added. The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 12 h and
quenched with 2 mL of 1N aq. HCl. After stirring for 1 h, the mixture was
diluted with Et2O (5 mL) and the aqueous phase was extracted with Et2O (3
x 2 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with water and brine,
then dried (MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure to
provide the crude product mixture. 1-(4'-Methoxybiphenyl-2-yl)pentan-1-ol
(4a). Following General Procedure A (using PdCl2(dppf) (3 mol%) and PPh3
(6 mol%) as the catalyst system), the product was purified by
chromatography on SiO2 (10% EtOAc/hexanes) to afford 4a (41 mg, 0.15
mmol, 50% from 8 (0.3 mmol scale)) as a pale yellow syrup. Analytical
data matches that which has been previously reported for 4aix. 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.60 (dd, J = 1.3, 7.8 Hz, 1 H), 7.39 (dt, J = 1.3,
7.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.29 (dt, J = 1.3, 7.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.24-7.19 (m, 3 H), 6.95
(d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2 H), 4.79 (dd, J = 5.3, 7.7 Hz, 1 H), 3.86 (s, 3 H),
1.77-1.62 (m, 3 H), 1.33-1.12 (m, 4 H), 0.82 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3 H); 13C
NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 158.9, 142.6, 140.6, 133.5, 130.5, 130.3, 127.8,
127.2, 125.9, 113.7, 70.5, 55.5, 38.6, 28.2, 22.6, 14.1.
