$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.3. General procedure A (in the Presence of
Ligand PN-1, Table 2) 4-Chlorobiphenyl (c9): The title compound c9 was
prepared following the general procedure A from the reaction of
phenyltriethoxysilane with p-chloroiodobenzene for 24 h and obtained as a
white solid (91 mg, 48% yield) after purification by silica gel column
chromatography using hexanes as an eluting solvent. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.41(m, 5H), 7.55 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 127.1,
127.7, 128.5, 129.0, 133.5, 139.8, 140.1; HRMS (APCI) Calcd for C12H9Cl
(M)+ 188.0393, found 188.0400.
