$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.3. General procedure A (in the Presence of
Ligand PN-1, Table 2) 4-Fluoro-4’-methoxybiphenyl (c13): The title
compound c13 was prepared following the general procedure A from the
reaction of (p-methoxylphenyl)triethoxysilane with p-fluoroiodobenzene
for 24 h and obtained as a white solid (93 mg, 46% yield) after
purification by silica gel column chromatography using hexanes as an
eluting solvent. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.86 (s, 3H), 6.98 (d, J =
8.7, 2H), 7.10 (t, J = 8.7, 2H), 7.50 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
55.5, 114.4, 115.7 (d, J CF = 21.2 Hz), 128.2, 128.3 (d, J CF = 7.9 Hz),
133.0, 137.1, 159.2, 162.2 (d, J CF = 244.0 Hz); 19F NMR (282 Hz, CDCl3)
δ -115.2; HRMS (APCI) Calcd for C13H11FO (M+) 202.0794, found 202.0795.
