$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.3. General procedure A (in the Presence of
Ligand PN-1, Table 2) 4-Methyl-4’-trifluoromethylbiphenyl (c11): The
title compound c11 was prepared following the general procedure A from
the reaction of p-(trifluoromethyl)phenyltri ethoxysilane with
p-iodotoluene for 24 h and obtained as a white solid (95 mg, 40% yield)
after purification by silica gel column chromatography using hexanes as
an eluting solvent. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.44 (s, 3H) 7.30 (d, J =
7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.52 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 7.69 (s, 4 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 21.3, 122.7, 125.8 (d, J CF = 3.5 Hz), 127.2, 127.3, 127.7,
129.8, 137.0, 138.3, 144.7; 19F NMR (282 Hz, CDCl3) δ -60.8; HRMS (APCI)
Calcd for C14H11F3 (M)+ 236.0813, found 236.0815. This product contains
approximately 5% impurity based on 1H NMR.
