$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3.4. Reaction of Phenyltriethoxysilane with o-Allyloxyiodobenzene In a
glovebox, o-allyloxyiodobenzene b21 (39.0 mg, 0.15 mmol), CsF (22.8 mg,
0.15 mmol), CuI (1.9 mg, 0.010 mmol) and the PN-1 ligand (3.0 mg, 0.01
mmol) were weighed in a 1-dram borosilicate vial and dissolved in DMF
(0.5 mL). Phenyltriethoxysilane (24 μl, 0.10 mmol) was then added to the
reaction mixture and tightly capped. The reaction mixture was then taken
out of the glovebox and placed in an aluminum heating block pre-heated to
120 °C with vigorous stirring. After 24 h, the reaction was cooled down
to room temperature, 20 μL of 2-nitrobiphenyl (0.010 mmol) as an internal
standard was added, diluted with EtOAc (1 mL) and filtered through a
short pad of silica gel in a pipette. The reaction mixture was then
analyzed by GC. The formation of the cross-coupled product c2 was
confirmed by comparison of the GC trace of the reaction mixture with that
of the independently synthesized and fully characterized standard sample
of c2. The product c2 was formed in 40% yield. The cyclized product d2
was not detected by the GC based on the comparison of the GC trace of the
reaction mixture with an independently synthesized and fully
characterized standard sample of d2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Hiyama coupling, sealed tube used
